tools: dictionary writer that handles stress and helper-call arms (Mudb0y tool sync)

Takes upstream tools/rules/newarm.py and tools/module/dict.py whole:
newarm learns the second arm shape (record pushed, helper called whose
name ends in the length), stress slots/values (stores stress patterns
into arms: 20100 is Appalachians), whole()/bypass/stresses/set_stress;
dict learns stress round-trip (dump writes it, read_file parses it,
build lays it) and stops reusing spare arms (a reused arm keeps the
replaced word's stress). Unblocks baking the names/smileys entries.
Tools only: nothing in the engine reads them at build time except
dict.py build, which CI runs explicitly.

